              "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 2)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "The chemical composition of 'slag' formed during the smelting process in the extraction of copper is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "rhEG7",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Cu}_2 \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{FeS}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "MutiU",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{FeSiO}_3$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "YZ3VV",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{CuFeS}_2$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "969MA",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Cu}_2 \\mathrm{~S}+\\mathrm{FeO}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "During the extraction of copper, iron is present in the ore as impurity (FeS).\nThe ore together with a little coke and silica is smelted; FeS present as impurity in the ore is oxidized to iron oxide, which then reacts with silica to form fusible ferrous silicate which is removed as slag.\n$2 \\mathrm{FeS}+3 \\mathrm{O}_2 \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{FeO}+2 \\mathrm{SO}_2 \\uparrow$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/6cK-T1m2YLKpiMG1exrlR_WDOlXvmbBGKhhiXVWaveI.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
          "previousYear": {
            "_id": "67726ce6d221dc77889e6415",
            "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
            "heldOn": "2024-04-15T14:00:00.000Z",
            "isVisible": true,
            "shortName": "2024 (Memory Based Paper 2)",
            "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 2)"
          },
          "evalStatus": "notAttempted",
          "lastPracticed": null
        },
        {
          "_id": "65b7b87397ae24e9e2db8c78",
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "65b7b85fb3be70ed63adbe84",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2023-04-15T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2023 (Memory Based Paper 1)",
              "title": "BITSAT 2023 (Memory Based Paper 1)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "The reaction that does NOT take place in a blast furnace between $900 \\mathrm{~K}$ to $1500 \\mathrm{~K}$ temperature range during extraction of iron is :",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "B6wMf",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Fe}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3+\\mathrm{CO} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{FeO}+\\mathrm{CO}_2$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "c4nnS",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{FeO}+\\mathrm{CO} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}+\\mathrm{CO}_2$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "PqP27",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{C}+\\mathrm{CO}_2 \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{CO}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "ATJU5",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{CaO}+\\mathrm{SiO}_2 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CaSiO}_3$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "At $900-1500 \\mathrm{~K}$ (higher temperature range in the blast furnace)<br />Reaction which take place are:<br />$\\mathrm{C}+\\mathrm{CO}_2 \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{CO}$<br />$\\mathrm{FeO}+\\mathrm{CO} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}+\\mathrm{CO}_2$<br />$\\mathrm{CaO}+\\mathrm{SiO}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CaSiO}_3$ (Slag formation)<br />$\\mathrm{Fe}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3+\\mathrm{CO} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{FeO}+\\mathrm{CO}_2$ at $500-800 \\mathrm{~K}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
