        {
          "_id": "64c0e80a6f5bfc7ab78aea0e",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7d",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2019-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2019",
              "title": "BITSAT 2019"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "The final step for extraction of copper from copper pyrite in bessemer converter involves the reaction",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "Mo6D6",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "bdUMm",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FeS</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "xKcXp",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FeS</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "crfeH",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>FeO</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>In Bessemer converter, copper-sulphide is partially oxidised to cuprous oxide, which further reacts with the remaining copper sulphide to give copper and sulphur di oxide, i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>This reaction represents auto reduction.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;reacts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>&nbsp;to give copper metal. The solid metal obtained is called as blister copper and is about 99% pure.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
